"rules.upgrade.class2.title" = "Rule conditions now read the rewritten request or status code";
"rules.upgrade.class2.body" = "When a rule’s conditions are evaluated, they read the request or status code as already rewritten by another rule, not the original. For example, after Map Remote changes the domain, a rule matching the original domain may no longer match; after a status code rewrite, a rule with a status code range reads the new status code. In each pair listed, one rule rewrites and the other’s conditions read the rewritten content.";
"rules.upgrade.class3.title" = "Multiple rules rewriting or mapping the same target (including Map Local Directory) now run in sequence";
"rules.upgrade.class3.body" = "Two status code rewrites: the later one overrides the earlier one. Two Map Remote actions: the later one continues editing the address changed by the earlier one. A Map Remote followed by Map Local or Map Local Directory: both run, and the response comes from the local file or directory. Previously only the first took effect and the rest were ignored.";
"rules.upgrade.pair" = "“%1$@” → “%2$@”";
"rules.upgrade.omitted" = "%1$ld more affected pairs of rules are not listed here.";
